-- Seed for SkillPassport App DB (production)
-- Creates the application user and the organization_staff profile of ALL 14 Soundarya trainers of the development educator seed
-- (dev/20261023100100_seed_soundarya_educators_skillpassport.sql), with the same user ids as the SSO accounts:
--   MBA with assignments: MOHAMMED SADIQ (Business Analytics), Ajay Kumar (Finance), Vishwanath Gurlhosur (Marketing), Poornima D U (HR)
--   MCA with assignments: Karthik Keyan, Suraj S P, Raghu B.N
--   Profile only (no assignment, session or task seed exists for them yet): Maheswari kumar, Visakh Madhu, Sandhya Mohan, Koutham K A,
--   Subashini Ramaswamy, Krishnalatha Atmakuri, Lalitha Srinivasan
-- Same rows as the development seed: the same ids, names, phone numbers, qualifications, experience and metadata (no value is invented; missing
-- values stay NULL). The user ids equal the development SSO ids, which the SSO production seed also uses.
-- Run AFTER the SSO production seed (sso-worker 20261023100000_seed_soundarya_trainers_sso_auth.sql) and BEFORE the MCA and MBA seeds
-- (20261023100200 to 20261023100700), which find each trainer by lower(organization_staff.email) in the platform organization.
-- The application user id MUST equal the SSO user id. An application user that already exists for an email is kept as it is (matched by lower(email)),
-- so run the PRE-CHECK first and make sure it carries the same id as the SSO account.
--
-- SSO LOGINS: the SSO production seed (sso-worker 20261023100000_seed_soundarya_trainers_sso_auth.sql) creates the login of the same 14 trainers, with the
-- same ids and emails. A trainer without an SSO account could not sign in, so keep the two seeds on the same list of trainers.
--
-- WHAT IS WRITTEN: public.organizations (platform organization, only if missing), public.users (14), public.organization_staff (14). organization_staff has
-- organization_type 'rareminds', role 'educator', account_status 'active' and metadata.teaching_access_enabled = true, which the teaching access check and
-- external_teaching_mapping_valid require. The staff table has no college column: the college (Soundarya Institute of Management and Science), the
-- class and the course are stored by the assignment seeds (organization_staff_assignments, 20261023100200 and 20261023100500).
-- Safe and idempotent: a trainer who already has a staff profile in the platform organization is skipped, so a second run inserts nothing.
--
-- NEEDS CLARIFICATION BEFORE PRODUCTION: Karthik Keyan's email below (karthikeyan201219996@gmail.com) differs from the Educator Details sheet of the
-- Soundarya workbook (karhitkeyan@rareminds.in). It must be the same email as in the SSO seed.
--
-- PRE-CHECK (read-only), run first, in the SkillPassport database and the SSO database. The ids must be equal in both:
--   SELECT u.id, u.email, s.id AS staff_id, s.account_status FROM public.users u LEFT JOIN public.organization_staff s ON s.user_id = u.id
--     AND s.organization_id = '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001' WHERE lower(u.email) IN ('msadiq.india@gmail.com', 'maheswarikumar27@gmail.com', 'cacsajay22@gmail.com', 'surajsp263@gmail.com', 'vishwanathgurlhosur@gmail.com', 'poornima.du@gmail.com', 'raghu.astepahead@gmail.com', 'visakh2013@rediffmail.com', 'sandhyamohan.sharath@gmail.com', 'koutham8505@gmail.com', 'subashini.r@rareminds.in', 'krishnalatha@rareminds.in', 'lalitha@rareminds.in', 'karthikeyan201219996@gmail.com');

